cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DueCare in academic work, cite the repository, exact commit, and dated evidence artifact."
title: "DueCare: A Gemma 4 safety ecosystem for migrant-worker protection"
abstract: >-
  DueCare is a local-first, open-source AI safety ecosystem built on
  Google's Gemma 4 that helps review recruitment fraud, contract
  substitution, passport retention, debt manipulation, and other
  trafficking-shaped patterns. One shared runtime supports six public
  setup lanes: Platform safety, NGO and regulator, Individual worker
  and mobile, Researcher, Anonymized knowledge sharing, and Developer
  and integration partner. The system combines deterministic rule
  checks, audience-aware prompts, versioned knowledge objects, local
  retrieval, reviewable tools, privacy gates, and replayable evaluation.
  Model synthesis is optional; deterministic extraction and provenance
  stay visible. Benchmark, dataset, and learning-study claims are kept
  in dated artifacts bound to their code commit, inputs, rubric, and
  model revision rather than embedded as mutable citation metadata.
